From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] misc: modem_v1: port the SS333 modem interface to Linux
 6.12 ARM32 (sec_modem_v1)

Lift-and-shift of the Samsung 3.10 modem_v1 driver (SIPC5 over MIPI-LLI
shared memory, SPI boot link, SS333 control) into one module,
sec_modem_v1, following research/modem/research/analysis/
kernel_port_design.md (KP) sections 1.2-2.8 and SYNTHESIS.md D1-D3, with
the blocking requirements of research/modem/research/review/
kernel_boot_review.md.  Every changed spot is marked "6.12 port".

API drift (KP 2.1): GPIO descriptors in raw physical levels (all lines
GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH in the DT, requested GPIOD_ASIS), wake_lock API on
wakeup sources (include/modem_wakelock.h), timer_setup, reinit_completion,
timespec64/local_clock, proc_create_single_data, __poll_t, netif_rx,
alloc_netdev(NET_NAME_PREDICTABLE), miscdevice attribute groups,
spi_delay, ioremap/ioremap_wc of the no-map region instead of a vmap of
struct pages, memcpy_toio/fromio and memset_io on shared memory,
%ps/%pS.  Dropped: link-PM FSM, ARGOS, IOSM/NAPI/SHMEM/C2C/HSIC/XMM/SS300
code, trace events, set_fs file helpers, gpio_export, lpcharge,
compat_ioctl, every panic/BUG site.

Safety (KP 2.8, review D1-a/d, D2-b, D3-a, D9-a):
- allow_hw (bool, default 0, root-writable, set callback): with 0 the
  probe completes and all nodes exist, but no line is driven, no IRQ is
  requested, no MIPI-LLI register is written and no SPI transfer starts;
  hardware requests return -EPERM.  0->1 (CP OFFLINE only) drives CP_ON,
  CP_RESET, PDA_ACTIVE, AP_DUMP_INT, AP2CP_STATUS, AP2CP_WAKEUP,
  IPC_INT2CP low in that order and requests the PHONE_ACTIVE and CP2AP
  IRQs disabled; 1->0 only while OFFLINE and unpowered.
- ss333_on/dump_reset release CP_RESET only after the SW_RESET_DONE of
  their own ld->reset with a correct remap readback
  (mipi_lli_wait_reset_done, 100 ms); otherwise CP_ON goes low and -EIO.
- ss333_off runs from any state and ends with CP_RESET low then CP_ON
  low (stock left CP_ON high), stock order and delays otherwise.
- SPI tripwire: the boot link sends only a 0x29FC-byte payload whose zlib
  CRC32 equals boot_crc (default 0x5DB1F04C), once per MODEM_ON; the real
  SIPC5 header length is stripped; the two 3.10 bugs (skb leak, error
  returned as 0) are fixed; spi_setup moves to the first transfer and the
  spi_driver is registered from module_init.
- CP2AP_WAKEUP/STATUS: edge-both IRQs, logged with a timestamp and
  counted, never acted on, disabled before any CP_ON/CP_RESET change,
  storm guard at 1000 edges/s.  Locked-on link PM replaces the FSM
  (SYNTHESIS.md D2): PHONE_START raises AP2CP_WAKEUP and AP2CP_STATUS and
  holds a wakeup source until ld->off.
- No system suspend while the CP is powered (wakeup source from MODEM_ON
  to MODEM_OFF, modem_suspend returns -EBUSY).
- dma_wmb/dma_rmb/dma_mb at every producer/consumer index of the legacy
  and SBD rings; shmem_map=device (default, ioremap) or wc.
- SIPC5_ALIGN pinned to 4 with a static_assert on sizeof(size_t).
- dflags 0 (mode 0644); umts_boot0, umts_ramdump0, umts_dm0, umts_router
  and ipc_loopback0 are 0600 root; IOCTL_MIF_LOG_DUMP only on umts_boot0
  and for CAP_SYS_ADMIN; debugfs svnet/mem_dump 0400; SIPC5 padding bytes
  are zeroed (3.10 sent uninitialised heap bytes to the CP).
- IOCTL_MODEM_CP_UPLOAD copies, logs, reports CRASH_EXIT and returns
  (cp_upload_panics=1 only requests an orderly reboot).
- No .remove, no module_exit, suppress_bind_attrs; .shutdown powers the
  CP off when allow_hw took the lines.

New: rmnet_type (rawip default, ppp stock), pm_mode (lockon only),
cp_status/value attribute group (cbd path), debugfs ss333/status (line
levels and directions, state, IRQ counters) and ss333/lli_reset (S2: LLI
soft reset with the CP off and in reset), MIPI-LLI and SPI probe
dependencies (-EPROBE_DEFER).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
